This stores `string[]` through a guard, which stores only a number, a `boolean`, an enum or a `string`, which the store copies, into a field or an element that already exists: anything else is a pointer, which may point into a task's arena, freed when the task is joined; build the value into the one the `Mutex` is made with, or store what it holds one at a time into slots that already exist, `g.value.names[0] = "x"`
